      "id": "3474299",
      "authorName": "(not exposed by CLI)",
      "postDate": "2026-06-17 19:00:15.950000",
      "votes": "60",
      "content_html": "<p>For this competition we'll be creating a dataset of the top episodes each day. This should help in reviewing replays as well as training agents. Each new dataset will be added to the index here: <a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kaggle/pokemon-tcg-ai-battle-episodes-index\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kaggle/pokemon-tcg-ai-battle-episodes-index</a></p>",
      "content_text": "For this competition we'll be creating a dataset of the top episodes each day. This should help in reviewing replays as well as training agents. Each new dataset will be added to the index here: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kaggle/pokemon-tcg-ai-battle-episodes-index"
    },
    {
      "id": "3481016",
      "authorName": "(not exposed by CLI)",
      "postDate": "2026-06-25 14:12:20.977000",
      "votes": "4",
      "content_html": "<p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/bovard\" target=\"_blank\">@bovard</a> \nThank you, this is really helpful!</p>\n<p>Could you add each team's score (rating) to the dataset? Right now the replay JSON only has the team names and the win/loss result (+1/-1) — there's no rating in it.</p>\n<p>For each episode, it would be great to have, for both teams:</p>\n<p>the rating before or after the episode</p>",
      "content_text": "@bovard \nThank you, this is really helpful!\nCould you add each team's score (rating) to the dataset? Right now the replay JSON only has the team names and the win/loss result (+1/-1) — there's no rating in it.\nFor each episode, it would be great to have, for both teams:\nthe rating before or after the episode"
    },
    {
      "id": "3482719",
      "authorName": "(not exposed by CLI)",
      "postDate": "2026-06-27 17:49:53.150000",
      "votes": "0",
      "content_html": "<p>Adding to this, I would want to have each agent's <code>agent_id</code> in the json file.</p>",
      "content_text": "Adding to this, I would want to have each agent's agent_id in the json file."
    },
    {
      "id": "3476832",
      "authorName": "(not exposed by CLI)",
      "postDate": "2026-06-21 02:54:36.917000",
      "votes": "2",
      "content_html": "<p>Thank you for all the valuable data!  If it is at all possible to share, what criteria is being used for which episodes get included in each day's index?</p>",
      "content_text": "Thank you for all the valuable data!  If it is at all possible to share, what criteria is being used for which episodes get included in each day's index?"
    },
    {
      "id": "3479295",
      "authorName": "(not exposed by CLI)",
      "postDate": "2026-06-23 16:14:57.993000",
      "votes": "0",
      "content_html": "<p>We rate the episodes by highest average participant rating. This will bias the dataset towards the episodes from the top competitors. </p>",
      "content_text": "We rate the episodes by highest average participant rating. This will bias the dataset towards the episodes from the top competitors."
